  "title": "Composing knots like cycles does not force rectangular knots",
  "subject": "The local converse of the difference-law characterization of circuit elimination",
  "conclusion": "The local converse and the diagonal lemma are false: a 3-variable knot on four values (x+y+z=0 mod 3 with 3 read as 2, minus (2,2,2)) is non-rectangular, yet its law composes every circuit like cycles because every system keeps the constrained sets of the Z3 law. Composition sees only which sets are constrained, so a dominating difference law hides any fibre pattern inside the components of a fibre graph.",
